WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.481
Email Writing.

2
00:00:01.761 --> 00:00:05.558
Day 60 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Workplace phase.

3
00:00:07.308 --> 00:00:08.332
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.612 --> 00:00:20.068
Today's goal: write clear, polite, professional emails that get a reply: the right subject line, the point first, one clear ask, and the right tone for managers, clients and colleagues.

5
00:00:21.418 --> 00:00:22.271
Part 1.

6
00:00:22.551 --> 00:00:24.301
The anatomy of a good email.

7
00:00:25.551 --> 00:00:26.468
Step 1:

8
00:00:26.748 --> 00:00:28.967
Subject: what it's about and what you need:

9
00:00:29.247 --> 00:00:32.553
Decision needed by Fri Payment provider for Q1.

10
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:33.751
Step 2:

11
00:00:34.031 --> 00:00:34.841
Greeting:

12
00:00:35.121 --> 00:00:37.020
Hi Priya, / Dear Mr.

13
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.900
Rao, / Hello team.

14
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.097
Step 3:

15
00:00:40.377 --> 00:00:44.623
Point first: the main message or request in the first 1 to 2 lines.

16
00:00:44.903 --> 00:00:45.863
Step 4:

17
00:00:46.143 --> 00:00:50.281
Details: short paragraphs or bullets: context, options, facts.

18
00:00:50.561 --> 00:00:51.521
Step 5:

19
00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:53.252
Clear ask + deadline:

20
00:00:53.532 --> 00:00:55.836
Could you confirm by Thursday 5 pm?

21
00:00:56.116 --> 00:00:57.055
Step 6:

22
00:00:57.335 --> 00:00:58.145
Closing:

23
00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:01.604
Thanks, / Best regards, + name (and signature).

24
00:01:02.954 --> 00:01:03.829
Part 2.

25
00:01:04.109 --> 00:01:05.773
Tone: choose the right level.

26
00:01:07.023 --> 00:01:08.388
Here is a quick table:

27
00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:14.705
Formal (client, senior, first contact), and Neutral (most work email), and Friendly (close colleagues).

28
00:01:14.985 --> 00:01:16.031
Dear Ms.

29
00:01:16.311 --> 00:01:17.015
Rao.

30
00:01:17.295 --> 00:01:18.959
Neutral (most work email):

31
00:01:19.239 --> 00:01:20.156
Hi Priya.

32
00:01:20.436 --> 00:01:22.057
Friendly (close colleagues):

33
00:01:22.337 --> 00:01:23.276
Hey Priya!

34
00:01:23.556 --> 00:01:25.455
I am writing to inform you that...

35
00:01:25.735 --> 00:01:27.399
Neutral (most work email):

36
00:01:27.679 --> 00:01:29.151
Just a quick update on...

37
00:01:29.431 --> 00:01:31.052
Friendly (close colleagues):

38
00:01:31.332 --> 00:01:32.143
Quick one:

39
00:01:32.423 --> 00:01:33.788
Please find attached...

40
00:01:34.068 --> 00:01:35.732
Neutral (most work email):

41
00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:37.036
I've attached...

42
00:01:37.316 --> 00:01:38.937
Friendly (close colleagues):

43
00:01:39.217 --> 00:01:40.305
Here's the file.

44
00:01:40.585 --> 00:01:42.356
I would appreciate it if you could...

45
00:01:42.636 --> 00:01:44.300
Neutral (most work email):

46
00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:45.625
Could you please...?

47
00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.527
Friendly (close colleagues):

48
00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:48.660
Can you...?

49
00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:51.265
Please do not hesitate to contact me.

50
00:01:51.545 --> 00:01:53.209
Neutral (most work email):

51
00:01:53.489 --> 00:01:55.367
Let me know if you have any questions.

52
00:01:55.647 --> 00:01:57.268
Friendly (close colleagues):

53
00:01:57.548 --> 00:01:59.169
Shout if anything's unclear!

54
00:01:59.449 --> 00:02:01.881
Yours sincerely, / Kind regards.

55
00:02:02.161 --> 00:02:03.825
Neutral (most work email):

56
00:02:04.105 --> 00:02:05.812
Best regards, / Thanks.

57
00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.713
Friendly (close colleagues):

58
00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:09.316
Cheers, / Thanks!

59
00:02:10.666 --> 00:02:11.562
Part 3.

60
00:02:11.842 --> 00:02:12.695
Templates.

61
00:02:13.945 --> 00:02:14.820
Request.

62
00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.977
Here is a template you can copy.

63
00:02:17.257 --> 00:02:18.132
Subject:

64
00:02:18.412 --> 00:02:22.380
Request: staging DB access for the coupon release (by Wed).

65
00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:23.599
Hi Arun.

66
00:02:23.879 --> 00:02:27.377
Could you give me read access to the staging database by Wednesday?

67
00:02:27.657 --> 00:02:31.007
I need it to test. the. coupon release planned for Friday.

68
00:02:31.287 --> 00:02:36.940
Details: user ashish.g, read-only access to the orders and coupons schemas.

69
00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:37.967
Thanks.

70
00:02:38.247 --> 00:02:39.079
Ashish.

71
00:02:41.929 --> 00:02:43.145
Status update.

72
00:02:43.425 --> 00:02:45.302
Here is a template you can copy.

73
00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:46.457
Subject:

74
00:02:46.737 --> 00:02:49.659
Weekly update, Checkout team (3 to 7 Nov).

75
00:02:49.939 --> 00:02:50.793
Hi all.

76
00:02:51.073 --> 00:02:54.742
Summary: on track for the 15 Nov release; one risk below.

77
00:02:55.022 --> 00:02:58.009
Done: coupon validation, 3 cart bugs fixed.

78
00:02:58.289 --> 00:03:01.766
In progress: delivery-slot API (70%).

79
00:03:02.046 --> 00:03:05.502
Risk: map vendor key still pending, needed by 10 Nov.

80
00:03:05.782 --> 00:03:10.539
Need: decision on slot-cache TTL (5 versus 15 min) from Priya.

81
00:03:10.819 --> 00:03:11.566
Thanks.

82
00:03:11.846 --> 00:03:12.678
Ashish.

83
00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.403
Follow-up.

84
00:03:16.683 --> 00:03:18.560
Here is a template you can copy.

85
00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.715
Subject:

86
00:03:19.995 --> 00:03:20.677
Re:

87
00:03:20.957 --> 00:03:22.643
API contract review.

88
00:03:22.923 --> 00:03:23.797
Hi Neha.

89
00:03:24.077 --> 00:03:27.811
Just following up on the API contract I shared on Monday.

90
00:03:28.091 --> 00:03:29.435
We need the review by.

91
00:03:29.715 --> 00:03:31.763
Thursday to. keep the launch date.

92
00:03:32.043 --> 00:03:35.883
If it's easier, I'm happy to walk you through it in a 15-minute. call.

93
00:03:36.163 --> 00:03:36.909
Thanks.

94
00:03:37.189 --> 00:03:38.021
Ashish.

95
00:03:40.871 --> 00:03:42.258
Apology or mistake.

96
00:03:42.538 --> 00:03:44.415
Here is a template you can copy.

97
00:03:44.695 --> 00:03:45.570
Subject:

98
00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:48.005
Correction: report sent this morning.

99
00:03:48.285 --> 00:03:49.202
Hi team.

100
00:03:49.482 --> 00:03:54.901
The report I sent at 9 am had the wrong date range (October instead of November).

101
00:03:55.181 --> 00:03:57.719
Please use. the corrected version attached.

102
00:03:57.999 --> 00:03:59.407
Sorry for the confusion.

103
00:03:59.687 --> 00:04:02.375
I've added a check so this. doesn't. happen again.

104
00:04:02.655 --> 00:04:03.402
Best.

105
00:04:03.682 --> 00:04:04.514
Ashish.

106
00:04:07.364 --> 00:04:08.324
Saying no.

107
00:04:08.604 --> 00:04:10.481
Here is a template you can copy.

108
00:04:10.761 --> 00:04:11.636
Subject:

109
00:04:11.916 --> 00:04:12.599
Re:

110
00:04:12.879 --> 00:04:14.671
Help with the analytics dashboard.

111
00:04:14.951 --> 00:04:15.932
Hi Rahul.

112
00:04:16.212 --> 00:04:17.620
Thanks for thinking of me.

113
00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:21.612
I can't take this on before the 15th because I'm on the. release.

114
00:04:21.892 --> 00:04:23.769
After that, I'd be happy to help.

115
00:04:24.049 --> 00:04:29.063
Alternatively, Kavya has built similar dashboards. and may. be able to help sooner.

116
00:04:29.343 --> 00:04:30.409
Best regards.

117
00:04:30.689 --> 00:04:31.521
Ashish.

118
00:04:34.371 --> 00:04:35.289
Part 4.

119
00:04:35.569 --> 00:04:36.849
Rules that save you.

120
00:04:38.099 --> 00:04:39.805
One email, one topic.

121
00:04:40.085 --> 00:04:43.776
Two topics, then two emails (or clearly numbered sections).

122
00:04:44.056 --> 00:04:46.680
Under 150 words for most emails.

123
00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.861
If it's longer, add a 2-line summary at the top.

124
00:04:50.141 --> 00:04:52.403
Bold the ask or put it on its own line.

125
00:04:52.683 --> 00:04:54.987
Reply all only when everyone needs it.

126
00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:57.656
BCC for large external lists.

127
00:04:57.936 --> 00:05:01.989
Check before sending: names, attachments, dates, time zones, tone.

128
00:05:03.339 --> 00:05:04.939
Don't write angry emails.

129
00:05:05.219 --> 00:05:08.249
Write them, wait an hour, then rewrite or call instead.

130
00:05:09.599 --> 00:05:10.559
Part 5.

131
00:05:10.839 --> 00:05:12.247
Phrases to replace.

132
00:05:13.497 --> 00:05:14.862
Here is a quick table:

133
00:05:15.142 --> 00:05:16.401
Instead of, and Write.

134
00:05:16.681 --> 00:05:17.982
Please do the needful.:

135
00:05:18.262 --> 00:05:20.118
Could you please approve the request?

136
00:05:20.398 --> 00:05:21.742
Kindly revert back.:

137
00:05:22.022 --> 00:05:25.499
Please reply by Thursday. / Let me know by Thursday.

138
00:05:25.779 --> 00:05:26.483
PFA.:

139
00:05:26.763 --> 00:05:28.150
I've attached the report.

140
00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.902
As per my last email...

141
00:05:30.182 --> 00:05:31.249
(sounds annoyed):

142
00:05:31.529 --> 00:05:34.643
As mentioned on Monday... / Just following up on...

143
00:05:34.923 --> 00:05:36.545
Sorry for the late reply.:

144
00:05:36.825 --> 00:05:38.147
Thanks for your patience.

145
00:05:38.427 --> 00:05:40.326
I hope this email finds you well.

146
00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:41.587
(overused):

147
00:05:41.867 --> 00:05:43.446
Hi Priya, (just start).

148
00:05:44.796 --> 00:05:45.735
Part 6.

149
00:05:46.015 --> 00:05:49.876
Conversation: asking a colleague to review an important email.

150
00:05:51.126 --> 00:05:53.153
Here is how the conversation goes.

151
00:05:53.433 --> 00:05:57.337
Meena, could you look at this email before I send it to the client?

152
00:05:57.617 --> 00:05:59.110
It's about the delay.

153
00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:00.094
Sure.

154
00:06:00.374 --> 00:06:00.993
Hmm.

155
00:06:01.273 --> 00:06:04.473
The first paragraph is all about the bank's API change.

156
00:06:04.753 --> 00:06:06.993
I wanted to explain why it happened.

157
00:06:07.273 --> 00:06:09.321
Put the new date and the plan first.

158
00:06:09.601 --> 00:06:11.777
The reason can be one line after that.

159
00:06:13.127 --> 00:06:14.727
The conversation continues.

160
00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:15.945
Good point.

161
00:06:16.225 --> 00:06:16.972
So:

162
00:06:17.252 --> 00:06:20.367
The payment feature will be ready on the 22nd.

163
00:06:20.647 --> 00:06:22.972
Everything else stays on the 15th.

164
00:06:23.252 --> 00:06:24.191
Much better.

165
00:06:24.471 --> 00:06:30.145
And make the subject line clear, something like Updated timeline: payment feature on 22 Nov.

166
00:06:30.425 --> 00:06:31.321
Got it.

167
00:06:31.601 --> 00:06:33.073
Should I say sorry?

168
00:06:33.353 --> 00:06:34.783
Yes, once, briefly.

169
00:06:35.063 --> 00:06:36.705
Then focus on the plan.

170
00:06:38.055 --> 00:06:39.655
The conversation continues.

171
00:06:39.935 --> 00:06:41.066
Thanks, Meena.

172
00:06:41.346 --> 00:06:43.650
I'll fix it and send it in ten minutes.

173
00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.939
Part 7.

174
00:06:46.219 --> 00:06:47.136
Practice.

175
00:06:48.386 --> 00:06:50.669
Rewrite this email to be clear and polite:

176
00:06:50.949 --> 00:06:52.463
Hi, PFA the doc.

177
00:06:52.743 --> 00:06:55.303
Kindly check and revert back ASAP.

178
00:06:55.583 --> 00:06:57.205
Also the meeting is shifted.

179
00:06:57.485 --> 00:06:58.487
Do the needful.

180
00:06:59.837 --> 00:07:00.755
Success:

181
00:07:01.035 --> 00:07:02.123
Sample answer.

182
00:07:02.403 --> 00:07:03.277
Subject:

183
00:07:03.557 --> 00:07:08.763
Review needed: payment design doc (by Thu) + meeting moved to Fri 3 pm.

184
00:07:09.043 --> 00:07:11.752
Hi Priya, I've attached the payment design doc.

185
00:07:12.032 --> 00:07:13.632
Could you review it by Thursday?

186
00:07:13.912 --> 00:07:17.645
Also, our design meeting has moved to Friday at 3 pm.

187
00:07:17.925 --> 00:07:18.992
Thanks, Ashish.

188
00:07:20.342 --> 00:07:21.878
That's the end of this lesson.

189
00:07:22.158 --> 00:07:26.830
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

190
00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:33.211
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

